// PSS v3.0 LRM — Example 266: Referencing PSS variables using mustache notation (page 352)
component top {
struct S {
rand int b;
}
action A {
rand int a;
rand S   s1;
exec body C = """
  printf("a={{a}} s1.b={{s1.b}} a+b={{a+s1.b}}\n");
""";
}
}

A variable reference can be used in any position in the generated code. Example 267 shows a variable
reference used to select the function being called.
